season five of my academia will be  animating a lot of great new characters  and quirks for the first time ever  so today i thought i'd do a quick  explainer video on one of the villains  that we'll be seeing  so the character for today's video is  getting and he actually made his debut  in the manga almost one year ago today  and since that first appearance there's  been a ton of fan speculation about him  with the most prominent theory being  that he is actually toyotaroki  and not darby i personally feel  confident in saying there's a 0.00001  chance of that actually happening but i  felt i shouldn't mention the idea  because it is the most prominent theory  about getting  and you know like i said there is the  tiny chance that horukoshi could troll  us and actually do something like that  but with that said  this video will not contain any plot  spoilers for season five but it will  explain his quirk and his philosophy  and i'm briefly going to touch on how i  think he would compare in a fight  against shoto  so do be sure to subscribe and let's get  into it starting with this quirk  it actually doesn't have an official  name yet so for the time being we'll  just call it ice bending  now contrary to what you might expect  this quirk does not allow him to  generate ice from his body  like it does for shoto but instead it  allows getting to freely control all  eyes within a certain range  now the range of the ice that he can  manipulate is pretty wide from this  panel in the manga we can see it covers  at least an entire neighborhood worth of  buildings  and given how much he's trained i would  estimate he can go much further than  that  with this power getting can warp the ice  into structures that support him in  battle  for example he can make a giant pair of  ice hands which he can then manipulate  as if they were his own hands or as we  see in this panel  he can seemingly shoot ice into the  ground which then propels him into the  air  other examples include shaping ice into  these shards which he uses to  one shot multiple people at the same  time and who could forget this slab  of ice which he uses to fly around like  the silver surfer  using a special strategy getting is  actually able to generate more ice if  the environment allows it  this quirk allows him to control the  temperature of any ice so that means  that he can send ice into a nearby  supply of water  whether that be a lake or maybe some  underground pipes and then by lowering  the temperature of the ice significantly  enough  the water around it then completely  becomes frozen as well and then he's  able to control that because it's now  ice  in the manga we see that his quirk is so  strong that once activated the ice just  comes flying straight towards him no  matter what's in the way  in this grocery store the ice literally  broke through the glass it was that  powerful  as a side note getting doesn't seem to  have any support items from what we've  seen he just you know wears this jacket  and this was surprising to me because  he's a character very much reliant on  his environment and you know how much  ice is nearby  so it would be really useful if you  could you know maybe carry around a few  cubes of ice in like a  tiny portable freezer that can fit in  your pocket just a suggestion but i  think something like that  would be really useful for him now  moving on to getting's philosophy  i'm sure some of you noticed in season  four but we briefly saw a glimpse of  this book which is titled the meta  liberation war  this book was written by a criminal  known as destro who is someone that we  saw earlier in the season during one of  gentle criminals flashbacks  destro believed that everyone in society  should have the ability  to freely use their quirks getting  himself is a firm believer in these  ideals  and he takes it a step further and  envisions a world in which people's  societal status is purely based  on the power of their quirk and the  group that getand has aligned himself  with in the series  also believe the same thing due to this  belief he's honed his quirk literally  his entire life and never actually  attended school  because he was too busy trying to master  this ability what this means is that  getting has trained longer with this  quirk  than most professional heroes which is  pretty crazy when you think about it  as a consequence of that getting has  amazing technique and also has a very  good perception of his opponent's  weaknesses and we'll be seeing that in  season 5.  however when we look at the ultra  analysis book his stats are not as great  as you would imagine with his technique  being rated a 4 out of 6  which for a guy who's practiced his  entire life is not really that great  i mean deku has a 5 out of 6 and he's  only had his quirk for like one year  but i will say in my personal opinion i  feel like the ultra analysis book  while it is a good reference point many  of the ratings are just absurd and don't  make too much sense  regardless of that we've had our fair  share of elemental quirks in this series  and i gotta say ice bending is  definitely one of the best it would have  been  seriously overpowered if he could  generate ice from his body but given  that getting isn't really meant to be a  boss villain  i think horikoshi did the right thing in  giving it the limitations that it has  bearing all that in mind how would he  compare in a battle against someone like  todoroki  i think it's pretty obvious that getting  completely nullifies the eyesight of  shoto's body  as any attack he could attempt to make  would automatically be turned against  him  from the perspective of shoto being  limited to justice fireside wouldn't be  too bad  as he'd still have the elemental  advantage as uh fire definitely uh beats  ice in a one-to-one match-up  that said getting isn't really the type  to be intimidated by  unfavorable matchup as he possesses an  unshakable faith in his abilities and  that's why i reckon if they fought each  other one versus one  as they are right now at least as long  as shoto doesn't know about the ice  bending ability in advance  i reckon that he'd use it and then get  him would catch him by surprise  and take him out before he had a chance  to rethink his strategy like i said  we'll be seeing him do his thing in  season five during the maybelline  academia arc  and i personally believe that when it  comes to his big fight that happened in  the manga  i think in that anime it will be  extended and drawn out a bit more  that's just my personal hope but i do  actually think it will happen  thanks for watching and i do have a  video coming tomorrow so be sure to  subscribe and turn on notifications  peace out
 

